  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="f-16" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Item 6 - &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="f-17" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Item 7 -&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="f-18" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Item 8 - &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The ratification of a new collective bargaining agreement on February 14, 2025 is estimated to have increased the Respondent's annual costs by approximately $0.8 million due to changes in wage scales for union employees, excluding fringe benefit costs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="f-19" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Item 9 - &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;There are pending appeals before the Kentucky Board of Tax Appeals of the Kentucky Department of Revenue's ad valorem tax assessments of the Respondent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock id="f-20" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Item 10 -&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock id="f-21" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Item 11 - &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;On May 25, 2022, FERC approved Respondent's uncontested rate case settlement reached with active parties effective November 1, 2021, which includes a limited Modernization program with cost recovery beginning March 1, 2023. On February 24, 2025, FERC approved Respondent's third annual filing establishing updated capital cost recovery mechanism surcharge rates effective March 1, 2025. The 2025 revenues associated with the capital cost recovery mechanism surcharges increased by approximately $3.0 million from storage customers and $3.1 million from transportation customers. These rate changes affected approximately 124 customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="f-22" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Item 12 - &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock id="f-23" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Item 13 - &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-24" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;1. CONTROL AND FINANCIAL STATEMENT PRESENTATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;Southern Star Central Gas Pipeline, Inc. (Respondent) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of Southern Star Central Corp. (Southern Star). Southern Star is a wholly-owned subsidiary of Southern Star Acquisition Corporation (SSAC), which is owned by Caisse de depot et placement du Quebec (La Caisse) and Ullico Infrastructure Southern Star Holdco LLC (Ullico).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements were prepared on a historical basis as required by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) in accordance with its Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases and do not reflect the application of purchase and pushdown accounting for acquisitions of the Respondent. The primary effects of purchase and pushdown accounting on the Respondent were the elimination of retained earnings and accumulated depreciation at the date of acquisition and the recording of goodwill for the excess of the purchase price over historical cost. Additionally, under accounting principles generally accepted in the United States (GAAP), certain other accounting classifications and disclosures are required which differ from those required by the FERC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;2. ACCOUNTING POLICIES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The preparation of the accompanying financial statements requires the Respondent to make estimates and assumptions that affect the amounts reported on the accompanying financial statements and notes. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;Revenues from services are recognized in the period the service is provided based on contractual terms and related volumes. The FERC regulatory processes and procedures govern the tariff and rates that the Respondent is permitted to charge to customers for its services. Key determinants in the ratemaking process are (i) contracted capacity assumptions, (ii) costs of providing service, including depreciation expense, and (iii) allowed rate of return, including the equity component of a pipeline&#8217;s capital structure and related income taxes. Accordingly, at any given time, some of the collected revenues may be subject to possible refunds required by final order of the FERC. The Respondent records estimates of rate refund liabilities based on its and other third-party regulatory proceedings, advice of counsel and estimated total exposure. See Note 3 for further information regarding revenue recognition. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;Regulatory Assets and Liabilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;As a regulated enterprise, the Respondent meets the requirements for accounting under the Regulated Operations Topic 980 of the Accounting Standards Codification (ASC 980). As such, certain costs that would otherwise be charged to expense are deferred as regulatory assets based on expected recovery from customers in future rates. Likewise, certain credits that would otherwise be recognized in income are deferred as regulatory liabilities pending potential refund or return to customers through future rates. Regulatory assets or liabilities are generally based on specific regulatory requirements or precedent for each such matter.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The following regulatory assets or liabilities are included on the accompanying Comparative Balance Sheets at December&#160;31, 2025 and 2024:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:27pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:81.101%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:55.597%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.084%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:19.266%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.084%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:19.269%"/&gt;&lt;td style="w