ckground-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;div style="padding-right:-1.88pt;text-align:right"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;8.13&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Rate to which the cost trend rate is assumed to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 7.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;decline (the ultimate trend rate)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;div style="padding-right:-1.88pt;text-align:right"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:100%"&gt;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;5.30&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;div style="padding-right:-1.88pt;text-align:right"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;5.15&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Period that the rate reaches the ultimate trend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2033&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:middle"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2032&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:middle"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;Other&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The Respondent maintains a defined contribution plan covering all employees. The Respondent&#8217;s costs related to this plan were $4.2 million and $4.0 million for the years ended December&#160;31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;8. MAJOR CUSTOMERS &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The Respondent is dependent on a limited number of customers for a significant percentage of our revenues and the loss of a large customer could have a material adverse effect on our operating results. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The Respondent&#8217;s two largest customers are Spire Missouri West (Spire), and Kansas Gas Service Company (KGS), a division of ONE Gas, Inc. Revenues, net of capacity released credits, received from Spire were $106.4 million and $105.9 million for the years ended December&#160;31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. Revenues, net of capacity released credits, received from KGS were $90.1 million and $90.0 million for the years ended December&#160;31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;Spire had a receivable balance of $9.1 million and $9.1 million as of December&#160;31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. KGS had a receivable balance of $8.0 million and $7.8 million as of December&#160;31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;9. RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The Respondent is a party to a Federal and State Income Tax Policy with Southern Star.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;In 2025, the Respondent paid dividends of approximately $101.3 million to Southern Star.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The Respondent utilizes a cash management program with Southern Star, whereby cash may be advanced to or from Respondent, to be repaid at any time as needed to fund operations. The advances earn interest based on the daily advance balance computed at the three-month U.S. Treasury rate as stated on the first day of each month. The Respondent had an advance to Southern Star for $19.1 million and $29.2 million at December&#160;31, 2025 and December 31, 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;10. NEW ACCOUNTING PRONOUNCEMENTS &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;On December 14, 2023, the FASB issued ASU 2023-09, &#8220;Income Taxes (Topic 740).&#8221; The amendments in this ASU require qualitative disclosure about specific categories of reconciling items and individual jurisdictions that result in a significant difference between the statutory rate and the effective tax rate. Disclosures will be required for income taxes paid (net of refunds), broken out between federal, state/local and foreign, and amounts paid to an individual jurisdiction when 5.0% or more of the total income taxes paid. The amendments in this ASU are effective for the Respondent&#8217;s annual reporting periods beginning after December 15, 2025. Management adopted this ASU as of January 1, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;On July 30, 2025, the FASB issued ASU 2025-05, &#8220;Financial Instruments&#8211;Credit Losses (Topic 326).&#8221; The amendments in this ASU provide all entities with a practical expedient and entities other than public business entities with an accounting policy election when estimating expected credit losses for current accounts receivable &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;and current contract assets arising from transactions accounted for under Topic 606. The amendments in this ASU are effective for the Respondent&#8217;s annual reporting periods beginning after December 15, 2025. Management adopted this ASU as of January 1, 2026. Management does not believe this ASU will have a material impact on the financial statements of the Respondent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;On September 18, 2025, the FASB issued ASU 2025-06, &#8220;Intangibles&#8211;Goodwill and Other&#8211;Internal-Use Software (Subtopic 350-40).&#8221; The amendments in this ASU remove all references to prescriptive and sequential software development stages throughout Subtopic 350-40. Therefore, an entity is required to start capitalizing software costs when both of the following occur: 1) management has authorized and committed to funding the software project and 2) it is probable that the project will be completed and the software will be used to perform the function intended. The amendments in this ASU will be effective for the Respondent&#8217;s annual reporting periods beginning after December 15, 2027. Management is currently assessing the impact this ASU will have on the financial statements of the Respondent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;On December 8, 2025, the FASB issued ASU 2025-11, &#8220;Interim Reporting (Topic 270).&#8221; The amendments in this ASU clarify interim disclosure requirements and provide additional guidance on what disclosures should be provided in interim reporting periods. The amendments in this ASU will be effective for the Respondent&#8217;s annual reporting periods beginning after December 15, 2028. Management is currently assessing the impact this ASU will have on the financial statements of the Respondent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;On December 17, 2025, the FASB issued ASU 2025-12, &#8220;Codification Improvements.&#8221; The amendments in this ASU include 33 codification changes that clarify, correct errors, or make minor improvements across a variety of topics. The amendments in this ASU will be effective for the Respondent&#8217;s annual reporting periods beginning after December 15, 2026. Management is currently assessing the impact this ASU will have on the financial statements of the Respondent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;11. SUBSEQUENT EVENTS &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;Management has evaluated all events or transactions that occurred from December&#160;31, 2025 through April&#160;15, 2026, the date these financial statements were available to be issued. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;On February 5, 2026, the Respondent entered into a treasury lock interest rate agreement that has a notional principal amount of $50.0 million. The treasury lock was terminated on March 17, 2026. The derivative settled unfavorably for less than $0.1 million, which will increase interest expense by less than $0.1 million over the term of the newly signed/committed debt.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;On March 17, 2026, the Respondent entered into a commitment for $150.0 million of 4.93% Notes which will be issued on May 28, 2026 and the proceeds of which will be used to pay off the Respondent's 4.66% Notes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-indent:27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;There were no additional subsequent events that required adjustment to the financial statements or disclosures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock id="f-25" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;Overhead Expenses Transferred&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;a)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:9.11pt"&gt;Nature of Overhead&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-22.99pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;i.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:18pt"&gt;The construction overheads include payroll and expenses for certain departments that impact capital projects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;b)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:9.11pt"&gt;Procedure for determining amount capitalized&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-22.99pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;i.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:18pt"&gt;Engineering &amp;amp; supervision construction overheads are charged directly to an overhead clearing work order, while administrative &amp;amp; general overheads are allocated to an overhead clearing work order via payroll journal on the basis of percentages derived from a time study. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;c)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;Method of distribution to construction jobs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-22.99pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;i.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:18pt"&gt;Construction overheads are allocated to construction work orders in direct proportion to construction costs incurred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;d)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:9.11pt"&gt;Different rates applied&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-22.99pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;i.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:18pt"&gt;Construction projects&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-25.21pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;ii.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:18pt"&gt;Other capital projects such as general plant and land projects&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-27.43pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;iii.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:18pt"&gt;Large construction projects&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;e)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:9.11pt"&gt;Basis of differentiation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-22.99pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;i.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:18pt"&gt;Construction projects receive administrative &amp;amp; general overheads and engineering &amp;amp; supervision overheads.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-25.21pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;ii.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:18pt"&gt;Other capital projects receive administrative &amp;amp; general overheads only.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-27.43pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;iii.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:18pt"&gt;Large capital projects receive reduced administrative &amp;amp; general and engineering &amp;amp; supervision overheads on direct charges greater than or equal to $10M.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;f)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:11.9pt"&gt;Overheads directly or indirectly applied&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:108pt;text-indent:-22.99pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;i.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:18pt"&gt;Overheads are indirectly assigned through the overhead work orders.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;2. &#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Allowance for funds used during construction capitalized on projects in the process of construction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;a.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;Allowance for funds used during construction is computed on all classes of property for projects where construction period is 30 days or more&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;b.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt; Half of the current monthly expenditures added to the balance of the previous month (excluding contract retainage and the allowance except for the semi-annual compounding of the allowance allowed by the Commission) comprise the base for the computation of the allowance at a rate of 9.10% per annum for all projects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;c.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:10.23pt"&gt;The computation period is from the date costs are first incurred until the facilities are placed in service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;d.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;The rate of 9.10% results from the use of the formula in Docket RM75-27, Order No. 561 approved on February 2, 1977.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;e.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;The AFUDC rate for borrowed funds after compounding is 1.75% and for other funds after compounding is 7.35%.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock>
  <ferc:ExplanatoryOfSecuritiesFinancingAndRefinancingTransactionTextBlock id="f-26" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;For additional information on financing, see Note 4 of Notes to Financial Statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:ExplanatoryOfSecuritiesFinancingAndRefinancingTransactionTextBlock>
